            <ArticleTitle>Are we being driven to two sensors?: clinical benefits of sensor cross-checking.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1441-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sensor cross-checking within dual sensor rate responsive pacemakers is designed to reduce the incidence of inappropriate rate response. We describe a patient in whom sensor cross-checking prevented the occurrence of angina during automotive transport.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
